## Context

Memo `conception/2026-10-31-monitoring-redesign.md` § 4.3. The one link not reconstructible from transcripts is which
session launched which headless child. Two launchers start them today:
`scripts/seat_clock.py run` (gaze seats: `codex exec`, `claude -p`, `pi -p`)
and `skills/manuscript-review/manuscript_review.py:462` (`claude -p` itself).
Neither records a parent. Part of tracker 1382.

Append one JSON line per seat to `~/archive/transcripts/<host>/launches.jsonl`
with `ts_start, ts_end, host, parent_runtime, parent_session, child_runtime,
child_session, seat, cwd, unit, exit`, through one helper both launchers call.
`parent_session` from `runtime.py session id`; Pi exports none today
(`scripts/runtime_session.py`): export it from the Pi adapter, or write
`not exported`. `child_session` is never a start-time join (gaze starts
same-runtime seats at once in one folder): pinned (`claude -p --session-id`),
the session file the launcher gave the child (Pi, aider, vibe under the
spool of 1383), or read from the child's output (Codex). The write is an append; a failure
warns on stderr and never changes the seat's outcome or exit code.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Test: a `seat_clock.py run` of a stub seat appends one well-formed line
      with the parent session id from the environment and the stub's exit
- [ ] Test: an unwritable launches file leaves the seat's status and exit code
      unchanged and prints one warning
- [ ] A claude seat's line carries the `--session-id` it was launched with,
      and that id names a transcript file
- [ ] One real gaze run on padme with a seat of each reachable runtime, and one
      manuscript-review run: every child appears with parent and child ids, each
      child id naming a transcript file (lines quoted in the PR)
